commit 3d22edcfc8ec871200e273ac206898d16b3c8d90
Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Sun Jun 14 01:14:43 2026 -0400

    fix(#12244) P2: crash-loop / session-limit respawn backoff
    
    The HealthPoller auto-reboot path respawned a dead agent instantly with no
    backoff. A Claude session/usage-limit exit-1 (or any fast-crash cause: stale
    lock, bad compose) became a tight respawn loop that burned a fresh session per
    spawn and looked like 'rebooting for no reason'.
    
    Add timing-based fast-death tracking to AgentState (last_spawn_at,
    consecutive_fast_deaths, reboot_blocked_until; in __slots__, to_dict,
    save_state, load_state). A death within FAST_DEATH_WINDOW (60s) of (re)spawn is
    a 'fast death'; FAST_DEATH_THRESHOLD (3) consecutive ones switch the reboot to
    exponential backoff (base 30s, cap 30m) and surface status='crash-looping' on
    /status instead of tight-looping. A dedicated resume branch respawns once the
    backoff elapses; a spawn that survives the window resets the streak (recovery).
    A one-off death (first fast death, or a long-lived agent) reboots immediately
    as before. Cause-agnostic — no parsing of claude's terminal output (which
    thin_launcher does not capture).
    
    Tests: 8 TestCrashLoopBackoff cases (below-threshold reboot, threshold backoff,
    exponential+cap, slow-death reset, resume-after-window, no-resume-before,
    recovery clears streak, state-file round-trip). 196 harness + 53 integration green.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

